{%- comment -%}
  This was a <div> carrying aria-label and an onclick. A div has no role, so
  the label was not allowed on it and nothing exposed it as something you can
  activate: keyboard users could not reach it, and Lighthouse's agentic
  browsing check failed the page on it.

  It is a link now, and a real one — the destination is built here rather than
  by waChat(), so it works with no JavaScript, opens in a new tab the ordinary
  way, and an agent reading the page can see where it goes. The setting asks
  for digits only, but a merchant typing +971 56 … is likelier than not, so
  the separators come out before the number reaches the URL.

  With no number set there is nothing to link to, so it falls back to a
  button and waChat()'s toast rather than rendering a dead link.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign wa_digits = settings.whatsapp_number | remove: ' ' | remove: '+' | remove: '-' | remove: '(' | remove: ')' -%}
{%- if wa_digits != blank -%}
  <a class="wa-float" href="https://wa.me/{{ wa_digits }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
     title="Chat with a human on WhatsApp" aria-label="WhatsApp support">{{ wa_svg }}</a>
{%- else -%}
  <button type="button" class="wa-float" title="Chat with a human on WhatsApp" aria-label="WhatsApp support" onclick="waChat()">{{ wa_svg }}</button>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  No chat launcher here: the Chizy app renders its own bubble, and chat-launcher
  styles in theme.css restyle it to match the theme.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="tfs-overlay" id="refOverlay" onclick="if(event.target===this)closeReferral()">
  <div class="tfs-modal">
    <button class="tfs-close" onclick="closeReferral()" aria-label="Close"><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">close</span></button>
    <div class="ref-modal">
      <div class="ref-icon"><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">redeem</span></div>
      <span class="label">Refer a Friend</span>
      <h2 class="ref-title">Give AED 30,<br><em>Get AED 30</em></h2>
      <div class="ref-offer"><span class="ref-give">Both of you save AED 30</span><span class="ref-was">AED 60 value</span></div>
      <p class="ref-sub">Share your link. Your friend gets AED 30 off their first order — and you get AED 30 in store credit the moment they buy.</p>
      <div class="ref-code-row"><input type="text" id="refLink" aria-label="Your referral link" value="thefragrancesecrets.com/r/SARA-30" readonly><button class="ref-copy" onclick="copyRef(this)">Copy</button></div>
      <a href="#" class="ref-share" onclick="waChat();return false">{{ wa_svg }}Share on WhatsApp</a>
      <p class="ref-terms">Credit applied after your friend's first delivered order. T&amp;Cs apply.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  The Custom Mixed Spray product, handed to the wizard in app.js.

  Every price and every variant id the wizard uses comes from here, so the
  storefront cannot quote a total the cart then disagrees with — it used to
  carry its own numbers in JavaScript, and a final button that called the
  demo addToCart() stub and added nothing at all.

  all_products returns nothing for a handle that is missing or unpublished,
  so this simply does not render in that case, MIX_PRODUCT stays undefined,
  and the PDP button (main-product.liquid) is not rendered either. The feature
  disappears rather than half-working.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign mix_product = all_products['custom-mixed-spray'] -%}
{%- if mix_product.handle != blank and mix_product.available -%}
  <script>
    window.MIX_PRODUCT = {
      handle: {{ mix_product.handle | json }},
      variants: [
        {%- for v in mix_product.variants -%}
        {"id": {{ v.id }}, "size": {{ v.option1 | json }}, "strength": {{ v.option2 | json }}, "price": {{ v.price }}, "available": {{ v.available }}}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      ]
    };
  </script>
{%- endif -%}

<div class="tfs-overlay" id="mixOverlay" onclick="if(event.target===this)closeMix()">
  <div class="tfs-modal mix-modal">
    <button class="tfs-close" onclick="closeMix()" aria-label="Close"><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">close</span></button>
    <div class="mix-head">
      <span class="label">Personalise It</span>
      <h3>Mix It Into <em>Your Spray</em></h3>
      <p id="mixHeadSub">We blend this oil into a ready-to-wear alcohol spray, made to order just for you.</p>
      <div class="mix-prog" id="mixProg"></div>
    </div>
    <div id="mixStepArea"></div>
  </div>
</div>

